# 4. HEADER AND SEARCH BAR

## 4.1 Header

Display:

- Hamburger menu on the left.
- Existing app logo or brand identity.
- Location icon toward the right.
- Favorites heart at the far right.

Use a white or very light gray background, balanced spacing, consistent icon sizes, and proper Android safe-area handling.

Reuse the existing shared header if one already exists. Do not create a duplicate header.

## 4.2 Search bar

Place a wide search field immediately below the header.

Suggested hint:

"Search for your car, e.g. Creta"

Include:

- Search icon on the right.
- White background.
- Light gray border.
- Rounded corners.
- Comfortable padding.
- Subtle shadow.

Reuse the existing search logic and data source. Do not invent a backend endpoint.

## 4.3 Pinned behavior

Keep the header and search area visible while the user scrolls, consistent with the intended design.

Use the existing app-bar or scroll architecture if it works correctly. Ensure the pinned elements do not cover content or conflict with Android system bars.

