# 17. NEWS, REVIEW, AND VIDEO CARDS

Display horizontally scrollable cards containing:

- Large landscape image.
- Headline or media title.
- Author, if available.
- Publication date, if available.
- Short summary, where applicable.
- **Read More** action.

Use white or very light gray backgrounds, subtle borders, rounded corners, and readable typography.

Prevent image distortion and text overflow.

## 17.1 Cars News

Use existing automotive news data.

Do not invent current stories, author names, dates, or article URLs. If no news source exists, use clearly identified sample content and document the missing integration.

## 17.2 Expert Reviews

Use existing review content if available. Otherwise, provide a documented placeholder.

## 17.3 Videos

Display actual video content when supported. Do not represent ordinary news articles as videos.

## 17.4 Read More

Open the existing article detail page or a valid source URL. Never invent a URL.

## 17.5 More News

Below the carousel, add a full-width outlined teal button:

**More News**

Navigate to the existing News page.

## 17.6 Avoid duplicate implementations

Before coding, inspect the News page, article models, media categories, services, and routes.

The New Cars page should display a small preview, not a second news database, news engine, or complete News page.

Both pages should reuse the same underlying data and article destinations wherever possible.

